{
 "tickets": [
  {
   "body": "Dear Billing Support Team,\n\nUpon reviewing our latest enterprise subscription statement for this month, I noticed an erroneous double charge applied to our account ending in 4092. We were billed twice for the same billing period on the 1st of the month. Kindly investigate this discrepancy and issue a full refund for the duplicate transaction back to our primary credit card on file at your earliest convenience.\n\nSincerely,\nBilling Department",
   "id": "gen-181",
   "subject": "Billing Discrepancy / Duplicate Subscription Charge on Enterprise Account"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi there, while updating our schedule visit types this morning, I noticed that several custom appointment durations were showing up on screens they shouldn't have. I want to make sure that our patient scheduling details and associated visit notes remained restricted properly and weren't inadvertently exposed to unauthorized staff or viewable across different permission levels. Could you please check our access logs or advise how to lock down those visibility settings?",
   "id": "gen-182",
   "subject": "Question regarding visit type visibility and permissions"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am trying to attach some scanned outside lab result PDFs to patient charts for review. Could you let me know what the maximum file size limit is and what the recommended format is for uploading these external paper documents smoothly? Thanks.",
   "id": "gen-183",
   "subject": "Uploading outside lab reports to patient charts"
  },
  {
   "body": "This is completely unacceptable. We just tried to transmit a routine maintenance prescription for a patient, but the system routed the entire order to a completely incorrect pharmacy location across town instead of the pharmacy listed in their favorites. To make matters worse, the dosage quantity was altered during transmission. We had to spend an hour on the phone sorting this out with the pharmacist while our patient went without their medication. I need someone to look into why this transmission failed and ensure our pharmacy routing rules are fixed immediately.",
   "id": "gen-184",
   "subject": "CRITICAL: Prescription sent to wrong pharmacy with altered dosage"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I'm checking our latest invoice and realized we were charged an incorrect amount for our software tier this month. We need this corrected and our account credited immediately as this is the second time this has happened.",
   "id": "gen-185",
   "subject": "Incorrect monthly charge on our account - need refund"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hi support, we are trying to get our front desk waiting room queue configured properly, but I am a bit confused by how the check-in timestamps are displaying. When a patient arrives and we mark them as checked in, the column sometimes shows the arrival time and sometimes shows the appointment time, and I cannot figure out which button or setting controls this view. Also, is there a way to add a custom status column for triage? I tried clicking around the settings menu under front desk options, but nothing seemed to change the layout on our main dashboard. Could you walk me through how to customize these columns correctly?",
   "id": "gen-186",
   "subject": "Waiting room queue status columns and check-in time display"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, I am writing to ask about managing our preferred pharmacy list for patients. When searching the directory for a local compounding pharmacy that recently opened near our clinic, it did not appear in the search results using either the zip code or the name. Could you please advise on how we can manually add a custom pharmacy entry into our local directory so our patients can select it for their electronic prescriptions? Thank you for your time and assistance.",
   "id": "gen-187",
   "subject": "Adding custom pharmacy entries to the directory"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, We recently encountered an issue where a medication substitution order was transmitted incorrectly to the local dispensary. The wrong therapeutic alternative was sent out on the electronic script for a patient. Please advise on the correct workflow to handle out-of-stock alerts and ensure future substitutions transmit accurately.",
   "id": "gen-188",
   "subject": "Medication substitution transmission error"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, We are currently performing an internal compliance review and need to pull system security audit logs for our facility. Could you please provide instructions on how our practice admins can export these logs to cover chart access over the past quarter?",
   "id": "gen-189",
   "subject": "Exporting security audit logs for compliance review"
  },
  {
   "body": "Hello, We are interested in configuring the online appointment booking feature for our patient portal so that individuals can schedule routine checkups and follow-up visits on their own. Could you please provide guidance on how to restrict this online booking capability to specific providers while excluding others, as well as how to limit which visit types are available through the public-facing portal? We want to make sure specialty consults still require staff approval before getting onto the calendar. Thank you!",
   "id": "gen-190",
   "subject": "Configuring online patient booking restrictions and visit types"
  }
 ]
}
